/T (The volume of goods transported along the corridor has since increased from around 350,000 tons to 530,000 tons between 2020 and 2021. However, what truly bolstered the corridor's utilization was Russia's invasion of Ukraine in 2022 and the subsequent economic sanctions imposed by the West on Moscow. )
