/T (The Caspian Sea level is the result of a certain balance between river inflows and evaporation, mainly; human actions also play a role, as well as possible tectonic movements. Some scientist project that by 2100, water levels in the Caspian Sea could drop by another 8 to 30 meters \(26 to 98 feet\). )
