/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The Caspian Policy Center \(CPC\) is an independent, bipartisan, non-profit organization dedicated to developing robust, pragmatic, and principled policies related to the economic, political, energy, and security aspects of the Caspian region. CPC actively engages policymakers, experts, and the public through innovative, evidence-based research, ideas, and analysis to shape and enhance discussions surrounding regional security and development.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
552 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Committed to upholding the highest standards of organizational, intellectual, and personal integrity, CPC maintains strict intellectual independence and exercises sole editorial direction and control over its research, projects, publications, events, and other activities. CPC does not espouse institutional positions on policy matters, and its publications reflect the viewpoints of their respective authors. In alignment with its mission and values, CPC refrains from engaging in lobbying activities and ensures full compliance with applicable federal, state, and local laws.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
553 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( )
/Pg 33 0 R
>>
endobj
554 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Moreover, CPC does not undertake representational activities or advocacy on behalf of specific entities or interests. Any funding received from non-U.S. sources is directed solely towards bona fide scholarly, academic, and research-related endeavors in accordance with relevant federal regulations. CPC also publicly acknowledges all donors who contribute annually on its website.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
